# Citation metadata, in the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.org).
# GitHub reads this and shows a "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo reads it
# when minting a DOI from a release.
#
# TWO THINGS TO FILL IN before this is used in a submission:
#   1. Uncomment the `orcid:` line below and put your ORCID in it.  Without it
#      the citation resolves to a name, which is not unique; with it, to you.
#   2. On each tagged release, bump `version` and `date-released` to match, and
#      add the `doi:` Zenodo mints for that release.  The version here should
#      equal the one a run log reports, or the citation names software that did
#      not produce the result.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ShelterDataPrep"
abstract: >-
  Config-driven preparation of animal shelter intake and outcome extracts for
  length-of-stay analysis.  A run is one YAML settings file, and produces the
  prepared data alongside a processing ledger that records every row removed or
  changed, a value-level breakdown of each filter and mapping, descriptive
  statistics of the finished set, and a provenance log.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mavrovouniotis"
    given-names: "Michael"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shelter-Data-Analysis/ShelterDataPrep"
keywords:
  - animal shelter
  - length of stay
  - data preparation
  - reproducible research
